{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA evidence for this ticket's acceptance criteria (from incident `bafc-2f85-836f-4bdd` / `decrepit-blowy-javalina`)\n\nTwo answers were requested. The second one **invalidates this ticket's replay criterion as written** — please correct it before anyone implements.\n\n### 1. Observed duplicate count and rate\n\nMeasured over the whole rebar store (5,329 non-archived tickets) and the live binding store (`.bridge_state/bindings.json` @ `origin/tickets`, 5,333 entries):\n\n- **89 normalized titles** have more than one ticket.\n- **425 excess tickets** (total copies minus one per title).\n- **425 of 425 are bound to Jira**, each to a distinct key — Jira range **REB-665..REB-4415**.\n- **389 of the 425** have rebar status != closed, i.e. they are the open Jira duplicates the operator sees.\n- Worst offenders: 12x `a2-1: move last_get_pass rotation bookkeeping...`, 9x each for seven `comment triage: <area>` titles, 8x several `size relief: ...` titles.\n\n**Rate, for threshold-setting:**\n\n| window | excess duplicate tickets created |\n|---|---|\n| 2026-08-31 (whole day) | 233 |\n| 2026-09-01 (whole day) | 172 |\n| peak hour 08-31 23:00Z | 88 |\n| 08-31 06:00Z .. 09-01 04:00Z (the burst) | 345 |\n| typical baseline (Jul-Aug, per day) | 0-2 |\n\nA threshold of **>10 same-normalized-title excess creations per rolling hour** separates the burst (88/hr at peak, 6 consecutive hours above 20) from baseline (0-2/day) with ~an order of magnitude of headroom.\n\n### 2. The duplicate signature — normalized title, as assumed. BUT the replay window is wrong.\n\n**Signature: confirmed normalized title.** All 425 were found by exactly `re.sub(r'\\s+',' ',title.strip().lower())` collision. `create_ticket`'s existing `duplicate_warning` (`_lib_writes.py:182`) uses the same signature and would have fired on every one. No rewrite of the criteria is needed on this axis.\n\nExplicitly ruled out, so nobody has to re-derive it:\n- **Zero** Jira keys are bound to more than one local ticket (5,333 bindings, 5,333 distinct keys). There is no \"one rebar ticket, two Jira issues\" duplicate class.\n- The binding store grew monotonically through the whole incident and never lost an entry, so there is no binding-field-only duplicate class either.\n\n**The replay criterion must change.** The ticket asks the detector to fire against store history for **2026-09-05 05:27-09:26 UTC** (the five long bridge passes). **Zero duplicate-title tickets were created in that window** — or anywhere in the 09-04/09-05 incident at all. A detector replayed there fires zero times and looks broken.\n\nThe correct replay window is **2026-08-31 06:00Z .. 2026-09-01 04:00Z**, where 345 excess creations occurred. Suggested criterion: replayed over that window the detector fires, and replayed over 2026-08-20..08-25 (baseline) it does not.\n\n### 3. A second detector is needed — title collision would NOT have caught this incident\n\nThe 09-04/05 event that produced hundreds of new open Jira issues was **~1,700 tickets with distinct titles** (`Condense comments in <path>`, one per repo file), created 2026-09-04 19:00-01:00Z. Every title is unique, so `duplicate_warning` is silent by construction and correctly so.\n\nThe signal that would have caught it is **creation volume**, not collision:\n\n- rebar side: local CREATE events/hour went 4-9 (steady) -> 62 -> 184 -> **968** -> 318.\n- bridge side: `RECON: outbound_differ create=` went 0-4 (steady) -> 138 -> 520 -> **1180**.\n\nBoth are rebar-side signals — neither needs a Jira query, so neither inherits the ACLI 1,200 ceiling. The `create=` counter in particular is already printed every pass and already thrown away, exactly like `duplicate_warning`.\n\nRecommend this ticket cover **two** detectors, or split the volume one out:\n- **A. Collision detector** — aggregate `duplicate_warning`; threshold >10/rolling hour; replay 08-31 06:00Z..09-01 04:00Z.\n- **B. Volume detector** — alarm on local CREATE events/hour and on per-pass `outbound_differ create=`; threshold ~10x trailing-7-day median; replay 09-04 19:00Z..09-05 02:00Z.\n\nDetector A alone would have missed this incident entirely. That is the \"quietly makes the whole alarm useless\" outcome the ticket was worried about, and it is real — just on the volume axis rather than the signature axis."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788621530184462718,"uuid":"d9e61719-91f9-4f23-99d4-a4a16ed250bf"}